% p2kb-pasm2-local.sty — P2 Assembly Language (PASM2) Reference per-manual override layer
% Loaded AFTER p2kb-platform-content.sty so anything here overrides platform defaults.
%
% PASM2 rides the shared platform stack (p2kb-platform-foundation + -content + the 5
% platform lua filters) for everything generic: the code boxes (IOSPBlock=green PASM2,
% Spin2Block, CORDICBlock, MultiCOGBlock, AntipatternBlock, SyntaxBlock), contmarkers,
% LayoutBlock/FormulaBlock keep-together, figure/table numbering, the \manualpart part
% mechanism + \chapter clearpage patch + \part styling, headings, and Shaded.
%
% This file holds ONLY what is genuinely PASM2-reference-specific — the instruction-
% reference apparatus that the local lua filters (p2kb-pasm2-entry-format,
% p2kb-pasm2-entry-headers) emit and platform-content does not define:
%   - entry-type header bars (instrheader / dirheader / constheader)
%   - the "At a Glance" box
%   - the 9-column encoding-table apparatus + inline encoding snippets
%   - the four reference admonition boxes (warning / note / tip / hardware)
%   - the Key Concepts box, instruction-entry container, related-instructions line
%   - syntax-display helpers, entry-heading helpers, enhancement markers, index helpers
%   - reference table column types and cross-reference helpers
%
% Definitions lifted verbatim from the retired p2kb-pasm2-content.sty so the reference
% look is unchanged from the pre-migration design. The four platform-owned sections of
% that file (part handling, DeSilva* code boxes, Shaded renew, \part styling) and the
% unused \lstdefinelanguage blocks were intentionally dropped — platform provides them.
%
% Package dependencies (tcolorbox, tabularray, needspace, enumitem, etoolbox, array,
% xcolor) are all loaded by p2kb-platform-foundation.

\NeedsTeXFormat{LaTeX2e}
\ProvidesPackage{p2kb-pasm2-local}[2026/06/10 P2KB PASM2 Reference per-manual override layer v1.0]

